20739 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Following Google\031s 2017 announcement of first\055class Android support\054 Kotlin quickly \050became known as \034the Android language\035 in most\240 developers\031 minds \023 associated mainly with mobile apps\056 \050\050In the years that followed\054 that association gradually became looser\054 driven mainly by backend adoption\056 And starting in the late 2010s\054 Kotlin\031s use as a JVM backend grew faster than its mobile base \023 JetBrains\031 2023 Developer Ecosystem Survey report described Kotlin\031s evolution from an Android\055focused language into a general\055purpose one\056\nBy 2025\054 data showed backend development had become Kotlin\031s second most popular \050use case\054 with over half of Kotlin developers using the language for backend\056 The language\031s footprint now extends into multiplatform\054 desktop\054 and web development\054 but the backend \050is the clearest single sign that the language is no longer defined by the platform that first popularized it\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 20740 0 R
     /Pg 3898 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

