20782 0 obj
  << /ActualText (A growing user base doesn\047t mean much if developers drift away after one or two projects\056 The data suggests Kotlin developers stay \023 and keep using the language year after year\056\nThe JetBrains Developer Ecosystem Surveys show that the number of developers having \050at least four years of Kotlin experience nearly tripled between 2021 and 2023\056 By 2025\054 \050the Kotlin Developer Survey found that about half of Kotlin developers have been using \050the language for at least three years\054 and nearly one\055third for five or more\056\nIn addition\054 satisfaction correlates with retention\056 The 2024 Kotlin Developer Survey suggested developers become more satisfied with the language as they use it more\054 \050with CSAT scores higher for experienced developers than newer ones\056 Developers adopt Kotlin\054 grow their expertise\054 and use it more widely as they discover what it enables\056\nTaken together\054 retention and rising satisfaction describe a mature ecosystem\072 \050Developers who adopt Kotlin tend to stay\054 deepen their expertise\054 and carry the language \050into their next projects\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 20783 0 R
     /Pg 4218 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

