20818 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Enterprise and Organizational Adoption\050\050Section 1 discussed Kotlin\031s takeup among individual developers\056 In Section 2\054 you\031ll see \050the picture at scale \023 with insights into how the language is used worldwide\056 Companies of \050all sizes\054 from solo developers to enterprises with over 5\054000 employees\054 are adopting Kotlin\056\050\050Kotlin usage isn\031t concentrated in a single company size\073 2025 Kotlin Developer Survey\031s 1\054532 respondents work across the full range\054 from solo practitioners to the largest enterprises\056\nAcross various surveys\054 independent developers are a large grouping\054 with some showing \050over a quarter of respondents identify as working for themselves \023 meaning that Kotlin has a strong following among individuals making their own choices\056 But the rest of the distribution is broad\056 In our own survey\054 small companies of 2\02350 account for nearly a quarter\054 mid\055sized organizations of 51\023500 for over 20\045\054 and larger enterprises of more than 500 employees account for another quarter\054 fairly evenly distributed across the 501\0231\054000\054 1\054001\0235\054000\054 \050and 5\054000\055plus bands\056\nThis even spread suggests Kotlin turns up wherever software is written \023 from startups choosing a modern stack to mid\055sized firms scaling their products and large enterprises maintaining substantial existing codebases\056 While this dataset is a snapshot and not a trendline\054 it shows the diversity of Kotlin adoption today\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 20819 0 R
     /Pg 5073 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
