20982 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Where do Kotlin developers come from\077 Overwhelmingly it\031s from the earlier language you\031d guess\072 Java\056 Across our State of Developer Ecosystem surveys\054 Java is consistently \050the language developers worked in before adopting Kotlin \023 by a wide margin\056\nAsked for their primary programming language before switching\054 over 70\045 named Java across surveys from 2022 to 2025\056 Earlier surveys\054 which asked a different question \023 whether respondents had used Java at all in their pre\055Kotlin days \023 showed even higher figures of over 90\045\056\nFor organizations\054 this is a practical advantage\056 Because the language shares a talent pool with Java developers\054 hiring and adoption risks are lower\056 Companies don\031t need to hunt for \034Kotlin developers\035 specifically \023 they can open the requirement to the vast Java\055savvy population \050or even redeploy the Java developers they already employ\056 This helps explain why Kotlin adoption tends to be incremental\054 moving from Java to Kotlin in stages\056\nBut there\031s a twist in the data\056 While the share arriving from Java is fairly steady \050declining just \050a few percent from 79\045 to 71\045 between 2022 and 2025 in our data\051\054 developers are also coming to Kotlin from Python\054 JavaScript\054 TypeScript\054 and even C\057C\053\053\056 And some never switched at all\072 In 2025\054 7\045 of Kotlin developers named it as the first programming language they ever learned \023 a hint of an ecosystem beginning to grow its own native talent\056\n)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 20983 0 R
     /Pg 7501 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

