21210 0 obj
  << /ActualText (While KMP is most often used to share business logic across applications and environments\054 teams increasingly seek to share user interface \050UI\051 approaches\054 too\054 improving consistency \050of the user experience across platforms\056 In Android\054 that\031s the job of Google\031s Jetpack Compose\054 the declarative UI toolkit for Android \023 a model that JetBrains has extended beyond Android with Compose Multiplatform\056\nWithin the KMP community\054 Compose Multiplatform adoption is near\055ubiquitous\056 In the 2025 KMP Survey\054 around 8 out of 10 KMP users reported using it for UI tasks \023 meaning that \050for many teams\054 sharing a common user interface\054 not just the logic beneath\054 has become part of the multiplatform value proposition\056\nSatisfaction has also kept pace as Compose Multiplatform adoption continues to grow\056 \050A large majority of users said the toolkit\031s feature set is sufficient for their needs\056 \050\050In UI frameworks\054 this is a high bar to clear\054 since missing components or platform gaps often block progress\056\051 We see consistent signals across different datasets that the ecosystem is becoming more capable and its users more confident in building full production applications\056 This suggests the toolkit is closing the gap between \034usable\035 and \034production\055complete\035\056\nCompose Multiplatform has become a core part of the KMP ecosystem\054 with rising satisfaction and a fast\055growing share of teams able to ship complete applications with it\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 21211 0 R
     /Pg 10478 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

