21235 0 obj
  << /ActualText (What do organizations actually get from KMP\077 The reported outcomes cluster around a single mechanism \023 writing code once for broader rollout across platforms\054 enabling downstream effects on speed\054 quality\054 and team\057task coordination\056 Here are some outcomes supported by data from JetBrains\031 Kotlin for Business and other sources\056\nBy sharing business logic\054 teams can write an estimated 40\045\02380\045 of their mobile codebase once rather than once per platform\056\050\nTeams also report 15\045\02330\045 faster release cycles after introducing shared logic\056\050\nFull return on investment is typically reached within three to six months\056\050\nAround 72\045 of users report improved development times\054 with a similar share stating improved project quality\056\050\nApproximately 55\045 report better collaboration between their Android and iOS teams\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 21236 0 R
     /Pg 11107 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

21236 0 obj
