21274 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Section 4 showed Kotlin reaching across platforms\073 In this section\054 you\047ll see it reaching across the stack\056 Backend development has become one of Kotlin\047s largest domains\054 with over half of Kotlin developers working on backend projects\056 \050\050That growth did not come from replacing Java systems\056 Kotlin compiles to the same bytecode\054 runs in the same JVM process\054 and calls existing Java code directly \023 so it spreads service by service through systems organizations already run and trust\056\050\nThis section draws on two kinds \050of evidence\072 what developers report \050in surveys\054 and what anonymized JetBrains IDE data shows about commercial organizations doing backend development\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 21275 0 R
     /Pg 11495 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

