21283 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The data leaves little doubt that backend development is a primary domain for Kotlin today\056 \050In our 2025 data gathering\054 over half of Kotlin developers reported working on JVM backend projects\056 More telling than the headcount is what they do with it\072 Nearly 80\045 of these developers run Kotlin in live production environments\054 not in prototypes or internal tooling\056\nThe backend work itself spans several critical layers of modern infrastructure\056 Among developers voting Kotlin their primary language\072\nOver 40\045 work on server\054 infrastructure\054 or cloud systems\056\050\nAround 40\045 build and provide APIs of their own\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 21284 0 R
     /Pg 11977 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

21284 0 obj
  << /K [ 21283 0 R ]
     /P 21311 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 11977 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

21285 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Surveys count developers\073 telemetry lets us also count organizations\056 In JetBrains telemetry\054 more than a quarter of commercial organizations doing backend development now use Kotlin on the backend \023 up from about one in five three years ago\056 And the larger the organization\054 the more likely Kotlin is already there\072 among companies with over a hundred backend developers\054 almost nine in ten have Kotlin somewhere in their backend today\056\nFor a decision maker\054 the two views compound\072 Kotlin on the server is production\055proven today \023 and in a large organization\054 adopting it rarely means going first\056 Someone nearby is likely already running it\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 21286 0 R
     /Pg 11977 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

