21687 0 obj
  << /ActualText (During and around KotlinConf 2026 \050late May 2026\051\054 we surveyed 623 active Kotlin users from an engaged\054 early\055adopter audience about how they use AI and how AI performs on Kotlin code\056\nThe dominant working pattern is to scope a task\054 let AI generate or edit the code\054 and then review\054 test\054 and iterate\056 Practically everyone validates the result \023 most review the code manually\054 and a majority also run it or put it through tests\073 just 0\0563\045 report shipping AI\055written code without any validation\056 AI speeds up the middle step of the loop\054 while the developer owns the other two\056\n)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 21688 0 R
     /Pg 17276 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

