21753 0 obj
  << /ActualText (What developers report is one kind of evidence\073 a public measurement is another\056 The Kotlin Benchmark\054 released by JetBrains in 2026\054 is an open evaluation of AI coding agents on real Kotlin software engineering tasks\056 It consists of 105 issues sourced from active open\055source repositories\054 where an agent has to read a real issue description\054 navigate the project\054 and produce a working patch\056 The benchmark applies the same standard developers apply to AI output \050see 6\0563\051\054 i\056e\056 a task counts as resolved only when the generated solution passes test verification in a containerized environment\056 All datasets and test harnesses are public\054 so anyone can compare agents on evidence rather than vendor claims\056\nLeading agents already complete a large share of the tasks\056 In the first public iteration\054 the top setup \023 Claude Code with Opus 4\0567 xhigh \023 resolved 90 of the 105 tasks\054 with JetBrains Junie \050Opus 4\0567 max\051 and Codex \050GPT 5\0565 xhigh\051 close behind\056 The scores are a signal\054 not a guarantee\072 Real\055world results depend on your architecture\054 internal APIs\054 coding standards\054 and validation process\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 21754 0 R
     /Pg 18351 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

