21809 0 obj
  << /ActualText (JetBrains\054 of course\054 is the creator of Kotlin\056 We built it\054 we maintain it\054 and of course we love it\056 That\031s why we always sense\055check our own data with broader developer surveys and independent sources like GitHub\054 Stack Overflow\054 and RedMonk\056 We accept we\031re not neutral observers\056\nBut according to multiple datasets\054 it seems the market agrees with us\056 The language has grown into a comprehensive ecosystem of applications both backend and front\055end\054 running services at enterprise level with confidence\056 And the newest test \023 whether a language holds up in AI\055assisted development \023 is one Kotlin is passing in public\054 on an open benchmark anyone can inspect\056\nOur philosophy is using the right tool for your needs\056 JetBrains AI tools \023 Junie\054 Air\054 JetBrains Central \023 work with Anthropic\047s Claude\054 OpenAI\047s GPT\054 Google\047s Gemini\054 or xAI\047s Grok\054 so you\047re never locked into a model provider you didn\047t pick\056 You can also point them at a local model on your own infrastructure\054 for full control\056\nSo whether you\047re adopting Kotlin for the first time\054 scaling it across teams\054 or wiring AI into a\240JVM backend\054 we\047d like you to try JetBrains tools in your own workflows \023 and judge them by the same standard we\047ve used throughout this report\072 what the evidence shows\056\nThat\031s Kotlin at 15\056 We look forward to improving it for many more years\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 21810 0 R
     /Pg 18751 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

