21818 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Many languages enjoy a few years of rapid adoption before plateauing or fading into a niche\056 Kotlin\031s defining characteristic is that its growth has been sustained rather than cyclical\056 It continues adding developers while retaining existing ones\073 it keeps moving into new domains rather than peaking in one\056\nAs we\031ve seen from our sources\054 Kotlin has become a general\055purpose platform\056 More than half of its developers now work on backend\054 nearly a third on multiplatform\054 and the language carries real production loads across finance\054 healthcare\054 and retail\056\nIts talent pool has matured\054 too\056 Two\055thirds of Kotlin developers have more than two years\031 experience\054 most have previous experience with Java\054 and a growing minority are Kotlin\055native\056 It\031s a diverse and flexible workforce \023 precisely what today\031s organizations need\056\nOrganizations also need a language that holds up in the age of AI\056 Kotlin does\054 for a structural reason\072 When machines write more of the code\054 the premium moves to verifying it \023 and Kotlin\047s strict compiler\054 strong type system\054 and production\055grade tooling catch mistakes regardless of whether a human or a model wrote them\056 The qualities that made it a safe adoption bet are exactly the ones the AI era rewards\056\nFifteen years in\054 Kotlin is an established part of the software landscape\072 broadly adopted\054 deeply trusted\054 and still extending its reach\056 If you\031re not yet using it\054 start at )
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 21821 0 R
     /Pg 19068 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

